# EAS ignores - prevents root workspace node_modules from interfering with the mobile build
# The mobile app is at apps/mobile/ and has its own node_modules
#
# IMPORTANT: leading-slash patterns are ANCHORED to the workspace root,
# so they only match the Next.js folders and never the mobile workspace's
# own apps/mobile/<same-name>/ directories. Without the leading slash,
# `src/` was unintentionally stripping apps/mobile/src/ from the EAS upload
# and breaking the cloud bundle (Metro could not find apps/mobile/src/...).
node_modules/
.next/
/services/
/src/
/prisma/
/scripts/
/docs/
/taste-skill/
*.md
.env
.env.local
